{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"electrical resistivity and conductivity units electrical resistivity and conductivity units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","fileName":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"electrical resistivity and conductivity units electrical resistivity and conductivity units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","fileName":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units","heading":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The book presents resistivity and conductivity as separate electrical conversion categories. Its resistivity example changes ohm-circular-mil per foot into nanoohm-meters, requiring resistance, area, length, and metric-prefix factors. Its conductivity example changes mho per centimeter into siemens per meter, converting the inverse-length denominator as well as the named conductance unit. The expressions Ω·m and S/m identify different target quantities; the shared electrical setting does not justify applying one category's factor to the other. See [[Conversion-Factor Chains]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"electrical resistivity and conductivity units electrical resistivity and conductivity units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","fileName":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Electrical Resistivity and Conductivity Units","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}